WEBVTT

1
00:00:18.269 --> 00:00:23.533
When we reached the grove of trees, I was amazed by the trees' great size and unusual appearance.

2
00:00:23.553 --> 00:00:28.516
"A house up there will be the safest and most charming home in the world," I said.

3
00:00:28.536 --> 00:00:31.638
"I knew you'd like it," said my wife.

4
00:00:31.658 --> 00:00:34.320
"Now I think we should prepare a meal."

5
00:00:35.484 --> 00:00:39.905
Ernest started fetching large, flat stones for a fireplace while Franz gathered wood.

6
00:00:40.665 --> 00:00:42.526
"What kind of trees do you think these are?"

7
00:00:42.846 --> 00:00:43.506
asked Ernest.

8
00:00:44.246 --> 00:00:46.547
"They must be mangroves or wild figs.

9
00:00:47.467 --> 00:00:51.328
I've heard of their great height and strange curving roots," I replied.

10
00:00:52.389 --> 00:00:55.489
Just then little Franz came up with a large bundle of sticks.

11
00:00:56.350 --> 00:00:57.770
He was happily chewing something.

12
00:00:59.670 --> 00:01:01.691
"Oh, Mother, this is so good!"

13
00:01:01.911 --> 00:01:02.291
he said.

14
00:01:02.311 --> 00:01:03.792
"What are you eating?"

15
00:01:04.112 --> 00:01:05.112
she cried in alarm.

16
00:01:05.920 --> 00:01:07.261
"It's probably poisonous.

17
00:01:07.521 --> 00:01:08.742
Spit it out right now!"

18
00:01:08.762 --> 00:01:11.183
"Where did you find this?"

19
00:01:12.044 --> 00:01:15.105
I bent down and saw what appeared to be a half-chewed fig.

20
00:01:15.125 --> 00:01:19.628
"There are thousands of them in the grass over there," said Franz.

21
00:01:19.648 --> 00:01:28.953
"These do appear to be fig trees, but you must never eat anything without showing it to me

22
00:01:29.093 --> 00:01:30.334
first. Promise?"

23
00:01:30.834 --> 00:01:31.334
I asked him.

24
00:01:32.495 --> 00:01:33.796
Franz nodded in agreement.

25
00:01:38.032 --> 00:01:41.833
After we ate, our first task was to make a rope ladder with wood steps.

26
00:01:42.753 --> 00:01:47.195
The older boys and I went to the beach to gather wood while Franz stayed behind with my

27
00:01:47.235 --> 00:01:52.456
wife. She started making harnesses for the cow and donkey.

28
00:01:54.617 --> 00:01:58.278
We soon had the ladder fastened securely to the tree above and the ground below.

29
00:01:58.298 --> 00:02:00.338
"I want to climb up first!"

30
00:02:00.618 --> 00:02:01.198
cried Jack.

31
00:02:01.218 --> 00:02:02.419
"Please, Father."

32
00:02:02.439 --> 00:02:04.939
"No, Father," said Ernest.

33
00:02:04.959 --> 00:02:10.242
"I should because—" "I'm the oldest," Fritz interrupted him to remind us.

34
00:02:10.262 --> 00:02:15.486
"Jack will have the honor," I said, "because he asked so nicely."

35
00:02:16.186 --> 00:02:18.168
Jack quickly sprang to the top of the ladder.

36
00:02:22.011 --> 00:02:23.231
cheers for the nest!"

37
00:02:23.552 --> 00:02:24.192
he exclaimed.

38
00:02:30.957 --> 00:02:35.060
I gave Fritz a rope to take up, and then Ernest and I followed him on the ladder.

39
00:02:36.220 --> 00:02:40.062
"Send up the pulley," I called to my wife as I dangled the rope next to the ladder.

40
00:02:40.882 --> 00:02:43.664
She tied the pulley to the rope, and I hauled it up.

41
00:02:45.304 --> 00:02:49.306
Then I fastened it to a branch overhead so it would be ready for the next day's work.

42
00:02:50.907 --> 00:02:52.428
We awoke early the next morning.

43
00:02:53.368 --> 00:02:57.030
My wife milked the goats and cow while the boys and I fed the animals.

44
00:02:58.450 --> 00:03:01.572
After that we went down to the beach to collect more wood for our house.

45
00:03:02.432 --> 00:03:06.414
We harnessed the cow and donkey to the larger beams and dragged the rest ourselves.

46
00:03:07.335 --> 00:03:10.216
Fritz and I then climbed the tree to finish the preparations.

47
00:03:11.057 --> 00:03:13.278
We cut many branches to clear a living space.

48
00:03:14.419 --> 00:03:16.620
But we left a few on which to hang our hammocks.

49
00:03:17.520 --> 00:03:21.142
Higher up, we kept some branches to support a sailcloth roof.

50
00:03:22.023 --> 00:03:26.145
My wife fastened the boards to the rope, and I used the pulley to haul them up.

51
00:03:27.786 --> 00:03:30.747
Fritz and I arranged the boards to make a smooth, solid floor.

52
00:03:32.988 --> 00:03:34.229
Then we built two walls.

53
00:03:35.550 --> 00:03:40.073
Our house was now enclosed on three sides because the great trunk formed a wall behind us.

54
00:03:41.014 --> 00:03:43.795
We left the front open to let in the fresh sea breeze.

55
00:03:44.736 --> 00:03:49.699
After attaching the sailcloth roof, our next job was to haul up our hammocks and hang them.

56
00:03:50.420 --> 00:03:53.802
We had been working all day, but a few hours of sunlight remained.

57
00:03:54.863 --> 00:03:57.645
Using the last of the wood, we made a table and benches.

58
00:03:58.525 --> 00:04:01.988
Finally Fritz and I, exhausted, threw ourselves on the grass.

59
00:04:02.940 --> 00:04:05.001
My wife arranged supper on our new table.

60
00:04:09.444 --> 00:04:11.485
We were just finishing supper when the pig appeared.

61
00:04:12.205 --> 00:04:14.146
My wife gave it all the milk that was left.

62
00:04:14.166 --> 00:04:18.428
"The milk will be sour before morning in this heat," she said.

63
00:04:18.448 --> 00:04:20.229
"You're right," I said.

64
00:04:20.249 --> 00:04:24.211
"The next time Fritz and I visit the wreck, we'll try to bring back a butter churn."

65
00:04:24.231 --> 00:04:27.573
"Must you really return to that dreadful wreck?"

66
00:04:27.873 --> 00:04:28.654
My wife shuddered.

67
00:04:28.674 --> 00:04:32.536
"You have no idea how anxious I am when you're there."

68
00:04:33.580 --> 00:04:36.261
"We must go back, but not tomorrow," I told her.

69
00:04:36.281 --> 00:04:37.942
"Come, it's getting late.

70
00:04:38.322 --> 00:04:38.983
Time for sleep."

71
00:04:39.763 --> 00:04:42.684
We lit our watch fires to keep away any wild animals.

72
00:04:43.825 --> 00:04:46.906
Fritz, Ernest, and Jack climbed up the ladder in a moment.

73
00:04:47.686 --> 00:04:49.327
Mother followed very cautiously.

74
00:04:50.388 --> 00:04:55.370
Although she had wanted to build this nest, she hesitated at the idea of sleeping so far off

75
00:04:55.410 --> 00:04:55.850
the ground.

76
00:04:56.570 --> 00:05:00.052
When she was safely in the house, I took little Franz on my back.

77
00:05:00.893 --> 00:05:03.941
I released the fasteners that held the lower end of the ladder to the ground.

78
00:05:04.703 --> 00:05:09.275
With the ladder swinging to and fro, we slowly went up, leaving the dogs below.
